    "extraction_notes": [
      "The supplied PDF SHA-256 is 9da993ff69f87d209649bbe4a5ff92bbf46f329889e749aa06f433300ee27c13.",
      "The 2N7002ET1G-ES is an N-channel device. Electrical characteristics are specified at TA = 25 degC unless otherwise stated.",
      "The output, transfer, capacitance, body-diode, and on-resistance points are manual digitizations of real curves in p. 4 Fig. 1 through Fig. 5; no fitted or interpolated vendor SPICE data was used.",
      "The published RDS(on) rows provide typical and maximum values: 1.85 ohm typical and 2.2 ohm maximum at VGS = 10 V, ID = 0.3 A; and 2.05 ohm typical and 3.0 ohm maximum at VGS = 4.5 V, ID = 0.2 A. All values are preserved as separate schema entries.",
      "The datasheet also publishes gate charge values QG(TOT) = 1.8 nC typical, QGS = 0.3 nC typical, and QGD = 0.6 nC typical at VGS = 4.5 V, VDS = 10 V, ID = 0.3 A; switching times are published at VGS = 10 V, VDS = 10 V, ID = 0.2 A, RG = 10 ohm.",
      "The datasheet publishes no reverse-recovery specification and no thermal junction-to-case table beyond RthetaJA typical 357 degC/W; those data are not represented by dedicated schema fields."
    ],
